   I just finished posting the latest version of PC NetHack (executable
and support files) to comp.binaries.ibm.pc. I went back and saved all
the parts (seven of them) and followed my own instructions on how to
extract everything, and it works. Any problems encountered while extracting
it shouldn't be my fault, so blame a noisy line or something.
   NetHack is a version of Hack, which is itself similar to Rogue. I'm
calling the version I posted 2.2-2.3 because it is somewhere between
versions 2.2 and 2.3 (which hasn't been released yet). Actually it's a lot
closer to 2.3 than 2.2, as I've fixed up the soldier code, and added 
barracks and a new type of trap, the land mine. Also, several bugs have
been fixed, including the inventory (et al) bug.
   I plan to keep a backup of the posting on my account here only for
a few days, due to limited disk space, so I won't be able to mail it to
anyone after Christmas. If someone is unable to get all the parts of
this I suppose I can let them send me a self-addressed stamped mailer
and two floppy disks (one if you can XARC it on your PC). Send me e-mail
and I can give you my US Mail address.
   Also, parts 1-7 of the posting are temporarily available via anonymous
ftp from iuvax.cs.indiana.edu, in directory pub/hack.
   Good luck on getting everything put together, and Merry Christmas!
(and any other holidays you may celebrate).

